# Pi workflow reference

Env-specific facts at their current state, dated; if behavior seems changed,
verify against the source repository and update this file. Sandbox, mode and
approval questions: `~/.pi/agent/docs/sandbox.md`; sweep measurements and audit
baselines: the chezmoi repo's `docs/agents-audit-log.md`.

## Launch and ownership (last verified 2026-09-07)

- Launch through the managed `pi` zsh function: it runs the repository's
  lockfile-pinned CLI (`node_modules/.bin/pi`) — no Brew install — disables
  native tools and ambient extensions, then loads the managed workflow and
  Herdr when present. A binary run outside it bypasses that.
- Pi loads the applied copy under `~/.pi/agent/workflow`, not the repository
  source; `~/.pi/agent/node_modules` symlinks to the repository's pinned
  `node_modules`, which pi's documented "node_modules in a parent directory"
  lookup follows. A source edit reaches a session only through `chezmoi apply`.
- The repository's npm manifest/lockfile is the single source for the CLI, the
  extension dependencies and the worker SDK — one pinned unit (currently {{ index (fromJson (include "package.json")).dependencies "@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent" }}),
  so CLI/SDK skew cannot occur. Pi breaks extension APIs across 0.x point
  releases: upgrade by bumping that one pin, then `npm ci`, `npm run test:pi` and
  `chezmoi apply`; the npm dependency hook installs with lifecycle scripts off.
- Settings are merged by managed key; unrelated UI/trust preferences survive.
  Authentication and session files stay unmanaged — sign in through Pi's normal
  OpenAI subscription login, and do not import another harness's auth files.

## Models (last verified 2026-09-23)

- Default: `{{ .agents.pi.defaults.provider }}/{{ .agents.pi.defaults.model }}`, {{ .agents.pi.defaults.reasoning_effort }} reasoning; planning uses {{ .agents.pi.defaults.plan_reasoning_effort }}.
- The approval classifier (MCP calls, remote-mutating shell verbs and unsandboxed
  requests) runs in two stages with no tools: `{{ .agents.pi.defaults.classifier_filter.model }}` at {{ .agents.pi.defaults.classifier_filter.reasoning_effort }} reasoning
  screens each reviewed action, and anything but allow goes to `{{ .agents.pi.defaults.classifier_judge.model }}` at
  {{ .agents.pi.defaults.classifier_judge.reasoning_effort }} reasoning on the same prompt; its verdict is final. Model, text and cache key
  align, but changing reasoning means cache reuse is not guaranteed.
- Worker tiers: {{ $sep := "" }}{{ range $tier, $model := .subagent_tiers.pi }}{{ $sep }}{{ $tier }} `{{ $model }}`{{ $sep = ", " }}{{ end }}.
  GPT-6 Sol serves both mid and top (2026-09-23): better than Terra 5.6 on score, tokens and cost per task; rationale and reversal in agents.yaml. Sol/Luna 6 accept `none` reasoning.
- The default is the frontier tier as the driver (shared `frontier_driver` rule in
  AGENTS.md, decision 2026-09-15). No child runs it: `workflow/children.mjs`
  rejects a launch naming or inheriting the frontier model and fails loudly;
  `general-purpose`, the only nesting role, is pinned to `top`.
- The pinned Pi SDK includes Astra in the OpenAI subscription catalog; if a
  future pin drops it, selection must report unavailable, not fabricate an alias
  or fall back to API billing.
